  "notes": {
    "about": "The art brief's keys (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-tactics-interactables-design.md section 4), as the manifest of a new set, content/tactics/base/interactables/manifest.json, in props/manifest.json's shape, so it loads with ArtManifests as it is: each kind's variants are its states (interactables.chest.open = ThingView.Art + '.' + ThingView.State), drawn as one frame each; each transition is an asset of its own, <kind>_<transition>, one strip played once from its first state to its last, then the state holds. Drawn at 1x, shown at 2x, facing sw; the TV mirrors for the other facings. ambient has no art of its own.",
    "anchor": "the ground contact pixel; stand it on the tile centre",
    "frames": "a transition is a horizontal strip, played once at fps",
    "cover": "none | half | full, for ranged attacks (a passage: when closed)",
    "height": "in height steps (16 px), for line of sight",
    "layer": "absent = over (a billboard, sorted with units); ground = lies flat under units",
    "blocks": "a passage's blocks is true and means closed: when open the engine says it doesn't",
    "empty": "a pickup's taken and a cache's open draw nothing: the TV isn't sent them, so they may be left out",
    "totals": "20 kinds, 41 state frames, 14 transition strips of 65 frames: 106 frames in all"
  }
}
